sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant S as TCP Socket Buffer<br/>(kernel recv / send buffers)
    participant CT as Controller
    participant W1 as Worker 1<br/>(primary replica)
    participant V1 as Volume 1
    participant W2 as Worker 2<br/>(secondary replica)
    participant V2 as Volume 2

    C->>S: HTTP GET /objects/:id
    CT->>S: async non-blocking read (network I/O)
    S-->>CT: HTTP request line + headers (object_id)
    Note over CT: Look up chunk metadata DB once:<br/>object metadata, ordered chunk list (seq_no, chunk_id),<br/>replica locations, per-chunk checksums
    CT->>S: write response headers: 200 OK, Content-Length, ETag
    S-->>C: HTTP response headers

    loop for each chunk in seq_no order
        CT-)W1: async HTTP GET /chunks (network I/O)<br/>object_id, seq_no, chunk_id
        activate W1
        W1-)V1: async read (disk I/O): chunk_id at offset, length
        V1--)W1: chunk data
        W1--)CT: chunk data
        deactivate W1
        Note over CT: Compute checksum of the received chunk (e.g. CRC32C)<br/>and compare with the checksum stored in the chunk map

        alt checksum matches
            Note over CT: Chunk verified
        else checksum mismatch, error or timeout from Worker 1
            Note over CT: Mark Worker 1 replica as corrupt<br/>and schedule background repair
            CT-)W2: async HTTP GET /chunks (network I/O)<br/>object_id, seq_no, chunk_id
            activate W2
            W2-)V2: async read (disk I/O): replica chunk
            V2--)W2: chunk data
            W2--)CT: chunk data
            deactivate W2
            Note over CT: Recompute checksum and verify again
            break replica checksum also mismatches
                CT->>S: abort connection (close / RST)
                S-->>C: connection reset, client sees truncated body
            end
        end

        CT->>S: async write of 1 verified chunk into the send buffer
        S-->>C: TCP segments carrying chunk bytes
        Note over C,S: Backpressure: a slow client shrinks its rwnd and the send buffer fills.<br/>The async write completes only when space frees up,<br/>so the controller fetches the next chunk only after that.
    end

    Note over C: All Content-Length bytes received.<br/>Client can verify the whole object against the ETag.
